{#
    Where everybody finished, on a screen where that pays nothing.

    <twig:FinishingOrder :rows="rows" />

    Rank, blader, record and form — and **no F1, bonus or total column**,
    because an unranked event writes no `TournamentResult` and there is no such
    value to show. A zeroed column would be the lie the invariant exists to
    prevent.

    **Used by the import preview, and deliberately not by the tournament page.**
    The proposal drew this block on both, but on an archived event the order it
    states *is* the ranking of the first stage — which the Swiss standings block
    already renders, with the record, the form and the tiebreak columns this one
    drops. A second table of the same entrants in the same order, minus columns,
    is a repetition rather than a summary. The preview is the case that stands:
    nothing is archived yet there, so this is the only statement of who finished
    where.

    `record` and `form` are optional. A row with no matches behind it keeps its
    place and shows a dash — which is every row on the preview, where the
    bracket has not been transcribed yet.

    The blader is named rather than linked. On the preview a row may be somebody
    the league is about to invent, so there is no profile to point at.
#}
{% props rows = [] %}

<twig:DataTable bleed>
    <thead>
    <tr>
        <th class="w-12 text-center sm:w-16">Rank</th>
        <th>Blader</th>
        <th class="text-center">W-L-D</th>
        <th class="hidden text-center sm:table-cell">Form</th>
    </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for row in rows %}
        <tr>
            <td class="text-center"><twig:RankMedal :rank="row.rank" /></td>
            <td class="font-bold text-ink">{{ row.name }}</td>
            <td class="whitespace-nowrap text-center font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">
                {% if row.matches > 0 %}{{ row.wins }}-{{ row.losses }}-{{ row.draws }}{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="hidden text-center sm:table-cell"><twig:FormStrip :results="row.form|default([])" /></td>
        </tr>
    {% else %}
        <tr>
            <td colspan="4" class="py-12 text-center text-sm italic text-ink-faint">This bracket recorded no finishing order.</td>
        </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
</twig:DataTable>
